 {"version_id": "prompt-03", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Mandatory test-driven convergence loop", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering", "replace": "After every nontrivial edit, run the narrowest relevant test or a focused reproduction, inspect the complete failure output, and iterate on the implementation until the focused checks pass. Then run the broader relevant test groups and, before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.88, "reasoning_soundness": 0.9, "execution_accuracy": 0.89, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.89, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.35}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.32}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.055, "why": "The mandatory focused-test and broader-test loop most directly repairs insufficient validation and iterative debugging, producing the strongest execution improvement. It still cannot compensate for an incorrect initial repository diagnosis, and mandatory testing can add cost or expose environment noise."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-04", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Failure-classification and escalation protocol", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering", "replace": "When a test fails, classify it as an implementation defect, an unmet edge case, an incorrect test assumption, or an environment issue; inspect the traceback and relevant runtime values, make one focused correction at a time, and rerun the smallest reproducer before expanding test scope. Do not finalize while unexplained failures remain; before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility revie"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.86, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.87}, "aggregate": 0.855, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.28}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.25}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.02, "why": "Failure classification encourages disciplined debugging and prevents blindly changing code, but it is less powerful than a full convergence loop and risks incorrectly labeling a genuine defect as an environment or test issue. Gains are therefore small, with target alignment slightly below baseline due to added decision overhead."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-05", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Expanded boundary and sentinel behavior matrix", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "normal inputs; empty and null inputs; minimum, maximum, and boundary values;", "replace": "normal inputs; empty, null, missing, malformed, and partially specified inputs; minimum, maximum, zero, negative, overflow, underflow, and exact-boundary values;"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.84, "execution_accuracy": 0.81, "output_integrity": 0.86}, "aggregate": 0.8425, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.27}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.23}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0075, "why": "A boundary and sentinel matrix usefully targets edge-case regressions, but the supplied change is fragmentary and broad rather than an operational validation procedure. It can encourage excessive or irrelevant cases without ensuring the implementation handles the repository-specific path, so execution and output integrity fall below baseline."}
+{"version_id": "prompt-06", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Compatibility-preserving differential review", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "For every row, state whether behavior must remain unchanged or intentionally change, then add or run a focused regression test for each affected row while preserving unrelated behavior.", "replace": "For every row, compare the old and new behavior explicitly, including return values, exception types and messages, ordering, mutation, numerical precision, serialization, and subclass or alternate-backend behavior. Mark each difference as required or accidental, add a focused regression test for every required difference, and add compatibility tests for nearby unchanged rows while preserving unrel"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.89, "reasoning_soundness": 0.89, "execution_accuracy": 0.86, "output_integrity": 0.91}, "aggregate": 0.8875, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.33}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.3}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0525, "why": "Differential review gives the strongest protection against accidental changes in exceptions, ordering, mutation, precision, serialization, and alternate implementations, substantially improving output integrity and regression handling. It is more reliable than the raw boundary matrix but remains dependent on having identified the correct old and new paths, so it trails the mandatory convergence loop on execution."}
